---
title: Threads
sidebar:
  order: 5
---

An EVT script can start another EVT script, or a block of its own commands, to run alongside it:

| Command | Waits for it to finish | Stops when this EVT script stops |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Exec(EVS_Other)` | No | No |
| `ExecWait(EVS_Other)` | Yes | Yes |
| `Thread` ... `EndThread` | No | No |
| `ChildThread` ... `EndChildThread` | No | Yes |

The new EVT script starts with a copy of the caller's local variables. After `ExecWait`, the caller gets the variables back as the other EVT script left them. The other commands don't copy them back.

For example, in an NPC's EVT script, this makes the NPC walk for a second while the partner talks:

```c
Thread
    Call(SetNpcAnimation, NPC_SELF, ANIM_Goombaria_Walk)
    Call(NpcMoveTo, NPC_SELF, 50, 0, 30)
    Call(SetNpcAnimation, NPC_SELF, ANIM_Goombaria_Idle)
EndThread
Call(SpeakToPlayer, NPC_PARTNER, ANIM_Goompa_Talk, ANIM_Goompa_Idle, 0, MSG_CH0_001C)
```

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `Exec(SCRIPT, ARGS...)` | Starts another EVT script and carries on without waiting. |
| `ExecGetID(VAR, SCRIPT, ARGS...)` | Like `Exec`, and stores the new EVT script's ID in `VAR`. |
| `ExecWait(SCRIPT, ARGS...)` | Starts another EVT script and waits for it to finish. |
| `Thread` ... `EndThread` | Runs the commands in between as a separate EVT script, alongside this one. |
| `ChildThread` ... `EndChildThread` | Like `Thread`, but the commands stop when this EVT script stops. |
| `AwaitChildren` | Waits until this EVT script's child threads have finished. |
| `KillScript(ID)` | Stops an EVT script. |
| `SuspendScript(ID)` | Pauses an EVT script. |
| `ResumeScript(ID)` | Unpauses an EVT script. |
| `IsScriptRunning(ID, VAR)` | Sets `VAR` to whether the EVT script still exists. |
| `AwaitScript(ID)` | Waits until an EVT script no longer exists. |
| `ExpectArgs(COUNT)` | Stops the game with an error unless this EVT script was given exactly `COUNT` arguments. |
| `SetPriority(PRIORITY)` | Sets the order EVT scripts run in each frame. Higher priorities run first. |
| `SetTimescale(SCALE)` | Speeds up or slows down this EVT script's `Wait` commands. |
| `SetGroup(GROUP)` | Puts this EVT script in a group. |
| `SuspendGroup(GROUP)`, `ResumeGroup` | Pauses or unpauses every EVT script in a group. |
| `SuspendOthers(GROUP)`, `ResumeOthers` | As above, except for this EVT script. |

## Arguments

`Exec`, `ExecGetID`, and `ExecWait` can pass arguments to the EVT script they start, which reads them as `ArgVar0`, `ArgVar1`, and so on. An EVT script can't change its arguments, and the EVT scripts it starts don't inherit them.

An argument is passed exactly as written, so a variable is passed as the variable itself rather than its value. To pass a variable's value at the moment the EVT script starts, wrap it in `ARG_INT` or `ARG_FLOAT`:

```c
EvtScript EVS_Jump = {
    ExpectArgs(2)
    Call(SetNpcJumpscale, ArgVar0, Float(1.0))
    Call(NpcJump0, ArgVar0, ArgVar1, 0, 0, 20)
    Return
    End
};

EvtScript EVS_Example = {
    Set(LVar0, 100)
    ExecWait(EVS_Jump, NPC_PARTNER, ARG_INT(LVar0))
    Return
    End
};
```
